"x4a0908tjv":"Transmit order (b0 first)",
"1czdyt4ifk1":"The encoding rules follow Section 5.3 of USB PD R3.2 V1.2: the Preamble is 64 bits of 0101… and is not 4b5b-encoded; all other data (including the CRC) is encoded nibble by nibble with 4b5b, each byte sends its low nibble first, and every bit is sent LSB first; SOP*, Reset and EOP use 5b K-codes directly. The CRC-32 uses polynomial 04C11DB7h, initial value FFFFFFFFh, a complemented result, and is sent low byte first. The waveform starts at a low level, and the end of the packet adds the closing edge and release to high impedance (Hi-Z) as the spec requires. The tool only handles the payload of ordinary (non-Extended) messages and does not model rise/fall time.",
"vgw4w8fem5":"Chapter 7. Protocol Message Definitions",
"17p861zduvq":"Every PD message is \"Preamble + SOP* + Header + Data Objects + CRC + EOP\".",
"1uk14vyoeth":"The Header is 16 bits and holds the Message Type, Spec Revision, Data/Power Role, MessageID and number of data objects.",
"p2ik2y5x5j":"Spec Revision: 01b is 2.0, 10b is 3.x (shared by 3.0, 3.1 and 3.2), and 11b is Reserved.",
"1awa6z7gi1o":"The receiver must reply with GoodCRC to every message; if it is not received the message is retried, at most 2 times (PD 3.x).",
