"1v8yo277koo":"Packet Structure Explained (Message Construction Breakdown)",
"13ctbneeyse":"A USB PD packet is made of the following 5 main blocks:",
"2b2l5wai0oy":"<strong>Preamble:</strong> a signal sequence used for synchronization and to indicate the start of a packet.",
"5nsx97y99b":"<strong>Header:</strong> the 16-bit core control header that defines the packet's attributes and the role state.",
"8funz8yvt8":"<strong>Data Objects:</strong> contain 0 to 7 data objects of 32 bits each.",
"1a3g4kpaipc":"<strong>CRC (cyclic redundancy check):</strong> used for error detection and to confirm data integrity.",
"bb1et8re4l":"<strong>EOP (End of Packet):</strong> marks the end of the packet.",
