"1da5ff9407j":"In Practice: Control Packets vs Data Packets",
"tmqnjs3ppb":"1. Control Messages",
"1l28p93tz67":"They contain only the 16-bit Header and no Payload, and are used for state control:",
"1zl9dpwvwv3":"<strong>GoodCRC</strong>: must be returned automatically within 195μs after a valid packet is received.",
"1xk1ayl27mx":"<strong>Accept / Reject</strong>: agree to or refuse a request.",
"1uz771wod0z":"<strong>PS_RDY</strong>: sent by the Source after the voltage transition is complete and stable.",
"1f3y0poh9r9":"<strong>Soft / Hard Reset</strong>: reset the state machine, or bring VBUS back to 5V.",
"11wq6rob8ll":"2. Data Messages",
"16dmoi7qa3h":"16-bit Header + 32-bit Data Objects:",
"1moqhwv2im":"<strong>PDO</strong>: a Source or Sink advertises what it can supply or consume (Source_Capabilities).",
"a489kg36xq":"<strong>RDO</strong>: the specific power request a Sink sends (Request).",
"11mtgprtzq9":"<strong>VDO</strong>: used in VDM packets for DP Alt Mode negotiation or reading the E-Marker.",
"1jn21qlkoab":"Chapter 8. PDO / RDO in Detail",
"24wmikiaxpk":"A Source advertises its capabilities with PDOs, and a Sink picks one with an RDO.",
"a3c6syx2lc":"PDOs come in several formats: Fixed, Battery, Variable and APDO (PPS, SPR AVS, EPR AVS).",
"1pkt7sth4cb":"The RDO's Object Position is \"which PDO\", counted from 1; Operating Current is the highest current the Sink will draw.",
"1xzd9khacp6":"The negotiation order is Source_Capabilities → Request → Accept → PS_RDY. VBUS has not changed at Accept; only PS_RDY means the voltage is in place.",
"bs60zv8j2a":"Reject means the request is refused, and Wait means try again later (wait at least 100ms).",
"1kynaeg1785":"Common misunderstanding: the RDO's Max Operating Current is deprecated and must be set equal to Operating Current.",
"s86o5od4ar":"Interactive tools: <a href=\"#ng\">Negotiation flow animation</a>, <a href=\"#po\">PDO/RDO decoder</a>",
"uqz7r492u8":"A Source advertises its supply capability through PDOs, and a Sink makes a specific power request to the Source through an RDO.",
"19gopgkm8uq":"<strong>Fixed Supply PDO (fixed voltage)</strong>: the 5V Fixed PDO must always be the first PDO a Source advertises.",
"11n7m71ivy5":"<strong>Variable / Battery / Augmented PDO</strong>: cover floating voltage, direct battery supply, and PPS/AVS.",
"21m2kfbp4az":"<strong>RDO (Request Data Object)</strong>: the Sink picks a PDO with Object Position and sets Operating Current and the Capability Mismatch flag.",
"1vyjocyw1g1":"Interactive Animation: PDO/RDO Negotiation Flow",
"7q0qwuseup":"From Source_Capabilities to PS_RDY, see how the Source and Sink go back and forth to settle on a voltage, and when VBUS actually changes. Below you can switch between four scenarios: normal negotiation, Reject, being told to Wait, and a lost GoodCRC that is retried.",
