"ezyuy6tsvq":"About 0.41 V",
"1fwyrizu3i3":"About 0.92 V",
"1dsvbgqc8oo":"About 1.68 V",
"7iiwvy6p07":"Interactive Tool: CC Voltage and Current Advertisement Detection",
"18sjircceiv":"The Source pulls CC up with Rp (or a current source) and the Sink pulls it down with Rd, so the voltage on the CC pin is the result of the two dividing. Adjust the Source advertisement, the pull-up method, what is connected on the other side, and the resistor deviation below to see which range the CC voltage falls in and what judgment the Sink and the Source each make.",
"1vmeq2jfob4":"Source advertisement",
"nwksdt29ac":"Pull-up method",
"6tw23klhj":"Resistor pull-up to 5V",
"26vals912xq":"Current source",
"y8yke7cexn":"What is on the other side of CC",
