"1hh3t31ekfc":"Hub's current draw (New Sink)",
"7ftfw1c38p":"Laptop supplies power (New Source)",
"2eau2rp4j4z":"① Starting point: the Hub supplies power, and the laptop is ready",
"1ientbcm0pp":"The Hub (Initial Source) is supplying power to the laptop (Initial Sink). The laptop has completed FRS initialization: the two sides have an Explicit Contract, the laptop has read the Hub's Sink_Capabilities and seen the FRS current field in the 5V Fixed PDO, and it has turned off Type-C disconnect detection.",
"1ct49krzdif":"② t = 0: the Hub sends the FRS Signal",
"pu477vgreg":"The Hub detects that external power is gone, immediately discards pending messages, and pulls CC low through ≤5Ω (rFRSwapTx) for 60–120µs. At the same time it stops supplying VBUS and instead draws current, with a current limit of iSnkStdby (500mA max).",
"1pyga2734yq":"③ About 30–50µs: the laptop confirms it received the FRS Signal",
"5fhhfkfwhj":"t ≈ 30–50µs",
"s4vqej6whp":"The laptop sees CC low for tFRSwapRx (30–50µs) and confirms an FRS Signal. It immediately stops drawing from VBUS, discards pending messages, and becomes the New Source.",
"x5ipxv0xan":"④ VBUS discharging (ms scale)",
"2eylsxv2tta":"A few ms (schematic)",
"5xho6xc38e":"In this case VBUS starts above vSafe5V (for example 20V). The Hub (New Sink) must draw enough current to discharge VBUS below vSafe5V (max) within tSafe5V (≤275ms). The laptop cannot supply power at this time and can only wait for VBUS to fall. This part is on the ms scale and is shown as a break in the diagram.",
"l8zxidqyvm":"⑤ Within 150µs after VBUS ≤ vSafe5V (max): the laptop starts supplying 5V",
"2f4qlp313me":"≤150µs after VBUS ≤ vSafe5V (max)",
"iq2n0mh291":"tSrcFRSwap starts counting from VBUS ≤ vSafe5V (max). The New Source must start supplying vSafe5V at the iNewFrsSink current within 150µs. This is done entirely by hardware; the TCPM reading and writing registers over I²C would never make it in time.",
"1vozcnqnlhr":"⑥ About 200µs: the Hub may draw iNewFrsSink",
"15z8wauraqo":"About 200µs",
"azfjny0wnq":"Only after tSnkFRSwap (≤200µs) may the Hub draw iNewFrsSink (Default USB, 1.5A or 3.0A, declared by the Hub in the FRS field of Sink_Capabilities). tSnkFRSwap starts counting from the later of \"the FRS Signal starts\" and \"VBUS falls below vSafe5V (min)\". Until the laptop's Rp is detected, the Hub must never exceed iNewFrsSink.",
"2aigcrrm273":"⑦ Entering the message phase: the laptop sends FR_Swap",
"1fpmln1tfh3":"A few ms later",
"2spj0sa262":"tFRSwapInit ≤15ms; on the Hub side tFRSResponse ≤50ms",
"y6qyae08fr":"The laptop (New Source) sends FR_Swap within tFRSwapInit (≤15ms) after detecting the FRS Signal. Counting from the FRS Signal, the Hub must receive this message within tFRSResponse (≤50ms), otherwise the Hub enters ErrorRecovery.",
"22c0l817xy5":"⑧ The Hub replies with Accept",
"kk48r1506n":"The Hub (New Sink) replies with Accept within tReceiverResponse (≤15ms). After the laptop sends FR_Swap, if it gets no Accept within tSenderResponse (24–30ms), it enters ErrorRecovery.",
"26xfckbf896":"⑨ The Hub applies Rd and sends PS_RDY",
"1vvpzi32lbh":"tFRSwap5V ≤15ms; on the laptop side tPSSourceOff 750–920ms",
"27obg767gk7":"After the Hub receives the GoodCRC for Accept and VBUS ≤ vSafe5V (max), it applies Rd and sends PS_RDY within tFRSwap5V (≤15ms), with the Port Power Role field set to Sink. On the laptop side, the PSSourceOffTimer (for SPR, tPSSourceOff 750–920ms) runs from the time Accept is received.",
"2fwx0zn0fqj":"⑩ The laptop applies Rp and replies with PS_RDY",
"28284yi5ta9":"After the laptop receives PS_RDY, it applies Rp (Type-C current ≥ iNewFrsSink) and replies with PS_RDY within tFRSwapComplete (≤15ms), with the Port Power Role field set to Source, and then re-enables Type-C disconnect detection.",
"227sj4u6cxb":"⑪ The Explicit Contract is re-established",
"1xe6f665ncp":"Afterwards",
"uv3bqn4epl":"Both sides enter an Implicit Contract, and the laptop sends Source_Capabilities (not the EPR version) to renegotiate. If the port was in EPR Mode, FRS also makes it exit. The whole FRS sequence is treated as one AMS, and an unexpected message received during it sends both sides to ErrorRecovery; if any step is late, the Hub may not be able to hold its internal power and shuts down.",
"f0tp2ppofm":"<text x=\"8\" y=\"20\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#2c3e50\">µs hardware zone (to scale)</text>",
