"676mdcetxe":"tDRP 50–100ms; Source time share 30%–70%",
"8q460t14vf":"Two DRPs have just connected",
"1mpb5h0qy7w":"Both sides toggle between Rp and Rd (taking turns as Unattached.SRC and Unattached.SNK). When one side presents Rp, the other is not necessarily presenting Rd, so it takes the two phases happening to line up.",
"1ny77d52mjj":"Phases line up: one side Rp, the other Rd",
"vjvf8o8ygs":"When the coincidence happens, the side presenting Rp detects Rd and enters AttachWait.SRC; the side presenting Rd detects Rp and enters AttachWait.SNK. The spec states that when two DRPs connect, whether the local port ends up Source or Sink is indeterminate. The clock used for DRP toggling also should not come from a precision timing source, to avoid both sides staying in phase forever and getting stuck.",
"y0erwh1iu8":"tCCDebounce 100–200ms",
"1ecw2sbtvii":"Connected after debounce, VBUS turns on",
"wl5ivtuqd":"The Source side sees Rd for tCCDebounce with VBUS at vSafe0V before entering Attached.SRC and turning on VBUS; the Sink side sees Rp for tCCDebounce and detects VBUS, then enters Attached.SNK.",
"r8j7no5asc":"Result: local A is the {a}",
"1pw723om2cz":"This time local A is the {a}. If your product must hold a particular role (for example a laptop that wants to be Source or a monitor that wants to be Sink), you need Try.SRC/Try.SNK or a later PR_Swap. Press \"Show another random result\" to see the other outcome.",
"r7h75pv1xj":"Local A (DRP, Try.SRC)",
"mpgvrjra6e":"tDRP 50–100ms",
"1srmlhkvnzr":"Two DRPs have just connected, and A prefers to be the Source",
"138y6qdhsx":"A has Try.SRC enabled, that is, it is a DRP that prefers the Source role. Before connection it behaves like an ordinary DRP, still switching between Rp/Rd.",
"71fyzshf22":"Collision: A is first assigned the Sink role",
"24gqe3otmso":"This time B presents Rp and A presents Rd: A detects Rp and enters AttachWait.SNK, and B detects Rd and enters AttachWait.SRC. Without Try.SRC, A would become the Sink.",
"101rjiwbc8q":"B turns on VBUS, and A was about to enter Attached.SNK",
"th6x65rwpu":"A sees Rp for tCCDebounce and detects VBUS, so it would normally enter Attached.SNK. But a DRP that prefers the Source role is allowed by the spec to enter Try.SRC instead and try once more.",
"2a51uuowbsn":"tSRCDisconnect ≤ about 20ms",
"1g1cjs5yh49":"A enters Try.SRC: Rd is replaced by Rp",
"fc6dtj2ibf":"A removes Rd and presents Rp instead, and does not drive VBUS. B no longer sees Rd on its CC and detects SRC.Open.",
"1otn9evzd2n":"tSRCDisconnect; VBUS falls to vSafe0V",
"1ckdq402jvu":"B gives up the Source role: VBUS off, and it presents Rd",
"k0nontbi71":"B detects SRC.Open within tSRCDisconnect. Because B is a DRP, it returns to Unattached.SNK and presents Rd, and VBUS is turned off along with it.",
"mshunjcwwu":"tTryCCDebounce 10–20ms",
"clumxbl92h":"A sees Rd and becomes the Source",
"1irncghjjd9":"A detects Rd in Try.SRC for tTryCCDebounce and enters Attached.SRC to supply power; B detects Rp and VBUS and enters Attached.SNK. A gets the Source role it wanted, at the cost of one VBUS interruption and a slower connection.",
"20hvndhse84":"Partner B (legacy charger)",
"12ry436cnwq":"A prefers Source, but the partner is a legacy charger",
"spv8453syo":"B can only be a Source and always presents Rp. A is a DRP with Try.SRC enabled and is still switching between Rp/Rd.",
"26tbtvxnw8v":"A connects as a Sink first, and B turns on VBUS",
"1bgt2pzt4eh":"A sees Rp in its Rd phase, and B turns on VBUS after seeing Rd. A detects Rp and VBUS and would have entered Attached.SNK, but a DRP that prefers Source enters Try.SRC instead.",
"bnvnxnxadv":"A removes Rd and presents Rp instead. B no longer sees Rd on its CC and detects SRC.Open.",
"2byg7kbia6j":"VBUS falls to vSafe0V",
"1fh0lq7y3yl":"B turns off VBUS, and A cannot find Rd",
"214otzizj3j":"B detects SRC.Open within tSRCDisconnect, turns off VBUS and returns to Unattached.SRC. B can only be a Source and never presents Rd, so A never sees Rd in Try.SRC.",
"25f73npdw7c":"tDRPTry 75–150ms; at most tTryTimeout 550–1100ms",
"53380yigpn":"No Rd found: A enters TryWait.SNK",
"1ymhcrs8wib":"After tDRPTry, with VBUS already at vSafe0V, Rd is still not detected (or at most tTryTimeout has passed), so A gives up the Source role, enters TryWait.SNK and presents Rd.",
"1opvzt0w7uj":"Reconnect: A becomes the Sink",
"1okp5459c45":"B sees Rd again and turns on VBUS again after tCCDebounce; A detects VBUS and enters Attached.SNK. A ends up as a Sink only. The cost is one VBUS dropout and a longer connection time, which is why a device with Try.SRC enabled causes one extra VBUS interruption when connected to a legacy charger.",
